## Builder brief (inlined from `work/docs/joola-sanity-page.md`)

Build Mudit's JOOLA case study page on a **review branch**, following this brief exactly.

### Goal

Ship a **full-case-study preview** at `/joola` that reads the unpublished Sanity draft **`drafts.joola`** (slug `joola`), renders BruinLease-style case-study primitives, and mounts **1:1 interactive prototype embeds** from `tidum41/joola-b2b-casestudy`. **Production** `/joola` stays the NDA gate only until the case study launches.

### Branch and PR

- Branch: **`review/joola-sanity`**
- Open a **draft PR**; **never merge** unless Mudit explicitly asks
- Report each shipped pass with: commit SHA, preview URL, verification commands run, artifact paths, and open gaps

### Sanity content

- Sanity project **`9vl5qk61`**, dataset **`production`**
- Draft document id **`drafts.joola`** (`caseStudy` type, slug `joola`)
- Map fields the same way as BruinLease (`app/ucla-sublease/page.tsx`, `lib/sanity/queries.ts`, `components/CaseStudy*`)
- Mudit approves all case-study copy. Use `[PLACEHOLDER: …]` styling for unfilled gaps (`JoolaSanityText`). Do not invent facts, metrics, or quotes (see `design/briefs/case-study-copy.md`).

### Draft loading (token + fixture)

Cloud agents often have **no** `SANITY_API_WRITE_TOKEN`.

1. **With token** (Mudit's `.env.local`): fetch draft via Sanity client with `previewDrafts` perspective and `SANITY_API_WRITE_TOKEN`.
2. **Without token:** when `SANITY_PREVIEW_DRAFTS=1`, load committed **`fixtures/sanity/drafts.joola.json`** (same shape as live draft). Keep fixture updated when draft structure changes.

Implementation: `lib/sanity/caseStudyDraft.ts`.

### Preview vs production

| Mode | How to enable | Page behavior |
|------|----------------|---------------|
| **Production** | Default on muditm.com | `ProductCaseStudy`: hero, metadata, NDA request only |
| **Local preview** | `SANITY_PREVIEW_DRAFTS=1` in dev | Full case study from draft/fixture |
| **Vercel preview** | `?sanity_preview=1` or header `x-joola-sanity-preview: 1` on preview deployments | Full case study without restarting with env |

### Section order and figures

Preview section order (TOC): **Problem → Solution → Research → Decision 1–4**.

| Section | Embeds / UI |
|---------|-------------|
| Problem | Copy only (before/after figure lives at **start of Solution** per Mudit) |
| Solution | Live quick-order portal iframe; before/after figure at top of section |
| Research | Copy |
| D1 | Quick-order line iframe |
| D2 | Row variant toggles (Compact / Reorder / Stock — product harness indexes `v=1,2,3`) |
| D3 | Review / checkout iframe |
| D4 | Approval toggles (Split inbox / Ledger) |

Use shared case-study chrome from BruinLease patterns. Hero embed chrome radius **8px**. Mock disclaimer above first interactive figure in preview.

### Prototype source (1:1 visuals)

- Product repo: **https://github.com/tidum41/joola-b2b-casestudy** (`live/` app)
- **Do not** ship CSS-cascade mocks from old PR #181 when product source is available
- Vendor product at a pinned SHA: `PRODUCT_ROOT=<path-to-live> npm run joola:revendor -- <sha>` (`scripts/joola-revendor.mjs`)
- Overlay patches: `scripts/joola-vendor-overlay/` — drop overlay copies of routes that now exist in the product harness (quick-order row variants, approval `Frame.tsx` exports, etc.)
- Build static embeds: `npm run joola:build-proto` → `public/joola-proto/round5/`, `public/joola-proto/qo/`
- Figures: same-origin **iframes** (`components/joola/JoolaProtoIframe.tsx`, `JoolaVariantEmbed.tsx`), uniform scale (`JOOLA_EMBED_DESIGN_WIDTH = 1280`), reserved height, URL/postMessage toggles without layout jump; no inner scrollbars; no cutoff at 390px
- Embed mode: `embed=1`, `HashRouter`, seeded buyer/admin state, no login
- **Pixel parity:** `npm run joola:pixel-diff` vs standalone proto; target **<0.5%** diff per figure; document in `artifacts/joola-sanity/`
- Dev single-figure bench: `/joola/parity?figure=…` with `SANITY_PREVIEW_DRAFTS=1`

Historical prototype refs (tarballs / branches): `cursor/round5-states-hierarchy-6235`, `cursor/qo-line-playground` — superseded by vendored `live/` at pinned SHAs when re-vendoring.

### Commands

```bash
# Default (production-like /joola)
npm run dev

# Full draft preview locally
SANITY_PREVIEW_DRAFTS=1 npm run dev

# Optional .env.local
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_PROJECT_ID=9vl5qk61
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_DATASET=production
# SANITY_API_WRITE_TOKEN=<Editor token>
# SANITY_PREVIEW_DRAFTS=1

npm run joola:build-proto
npm run typecheck && npm run build
SANITY_PREVIEW_DRAFTS=1 npm run dev
npm run joola:pixel-diff
```

Lint may be broken on Next 16; use `npm run typecheck` as the gate (`AGENTS.md`).

### Verification report

Update `artifacts/joola-sanity/REPORT.md` when architecture or diff results change. Commit capture assets under `artifacts/joola-sanity/` (pixel-diff triplets, preview screenshots).

For each delivery note:

- SHA and preview URL (Vercel portfolio **READY**)
- Whether hosted `drafts.joola` was patched or only fixture
- Pixel-diff table or per-iframe DOM grep when embeds change
- Screenshot paths

### Product content constraints (case study + embeds)

Follow Mudit's product decisions unless brief says otherwise: **Dick's Sporting Goods** account in hero, status lifecycle, **no cases / no tiers** in approved copy, **Saved for reorder** naming. Single account price per SKU in line UI. Do not reintroduce tier/volume or case-pack UI removed from approved builds unless Mudit asks.

When re-vendoring, verify embed DOM across **9 iframes** at **1440** and **1024** (chips, Upload CSV, warehouse names, template, middle dot, case/tier strings, nav icon **x=20** / label **x=44**). Some strings may remain in **product source** (not overlay); report honestly.
